## Table metadata counts DESCRIBE section rows as columns
================================================================================

Context:
On workspaces with automatic liquid clustering, DESCRIBE <table> appends a
"# Clustering Information" section that repeats the clustering columns
("# col_name | data_type | comment" header, then one row per column).
Partitioned tables do the same with a blank row and "# Partition
Information". UnityCatalog.get_table_columns() returned every row, so the
Data Assets page showed two phantom columns per table (463 columns instead
of 373 on a 45-table schema) and reported 45 columns "missing
descriptions" even though every real column had a comment. The phantom rows
also reached mapping and ontology generation as if they were columns.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/databricks/uc/UnityCatalog.py
   get_table_columns() stops at the first DESCRIBE row whose name is empty
   or starts with "#", i.e. where a metadata section begins.
2. tests/units/core/test_unity_catalog.py
   New tests: clustering section rows and partition section rows (with the
   blank separator) are not returned as columns.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/databricks/uc/UnityCatalog.py
- tests/units/core/test_unity_catalog.py
- changelogs/v0.9.0/simyung-yang_2026-10-27.log

