## Fix: schema-access check crashed on dict-row cursors
================================================================================

Context:
The managed-synced Build failed at "Creating companion table" with
"Could not prepare Lakebase companion table: 0". The graph store cursor uses
psycopg dict_row, so ensure_schema_writable's row[0] raised KeyError(0). The
unit tests used tuple rows and missed it.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/_companion_ddl.py
   ensure_schema_writable selects a row only when USAGE and CREATE are held
   and checks row presence, like the pgcrypto check, so it works with dict
   and tuple cursors.
2. tests/units/core/test_companion_ddl_schema_access.py,
   tests/units/core/test_lakebase_flat_store.py
   Fixtures follow the row-presence contract; the success case uses a
   dict row.

