## Global config: a failed read is no longer cached or saved as the config
================================================================================

Context:
Graph Chat answered "graph does not exist yet" for a built graph, the chat
header showed "not built", and the branding fell back to the default title.
One global-config read failed (Lakebase compute waking from scale-to-zero).
The service cached the empty template for the full 5-minute TTL. A later
failure then served that template as the last good config for up to
30 minutes. Without graph_engine_config.schema, the Lakebase store fell back
to the registry schema name and queried a schema with no graph tables. A save
in that window would also have written the template over the stored config.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/session/GlobalConfigService.py
   - Track whether the cache came from a successful read (_cache_ok).
   - After a failed read, keep the empty template for
     _FAILED_LOAD_RETRY_S (10 s) only, then read again.
   - Serve a stale cache on failure only when it came from a successful read.
     A failure past the stale window is marked as failed.
   - _save refuses to write when the current config could not be read.
     A first save on an empty registry is still allowed.
   - set_ui_branding only reuses the cache when it came from a successful
     read.
2. tests/units/settings/test_graph_engine_config.py
   New TestGlobalConfigFailedLoad: retry after a failed read, no promotion
   to stale, failure past the stale window, refused save, first save allowed.
3. tests/units/settings/test_ui_branding.py
   The patched load marks the read as successful (new save contract).

Modified files:
- src/back/objects/session/GlobalConfigService.py
- tests/units/settings/test_graph_engine_config.py
- tests/units/settings/test_ui_branding.py
- changelogs/v0.9.0/simyung-yang_2026-10-27.log

