## Auto-mapping: subclasses are narrowed to their own rows
================================================================================

Context:
Auto-mapping sent the agent only each entity's URI, label and attributes.
A subclass (e.g. "equipment unit" under Equipment, or "defect code" under
Reason) was then often mapped to every row of its parent's table. Nothing
told the agent that it was a subset, and the class description, which states
the selection criterion, was not sent. Subclasses whose label implied a
filter were mapped correctly; the others were not.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-autoassign.js,
   src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-design.js
   The three agent entity payloads (bulk, partial-attribute and single-item
   auto-map) now include parent and description (the class comment). The
   route, service and get_ontology tool already pass entity dicts through.
2. src/agents/agent_auto_assignment/engine.py (SYSTEM_PROMPT)
   New SUBCLASSES rules:
   - Read each entity's description.
   - A subclass query returns only the subclass rows, using the criterion
     stated in the description or a type / level / category column, and the
     split is checked with execute_sql.
   - If no column separates the subclass, report that in the summary.
3. tests/units/mapping/test_auto_assign_subclass_context.py
   New contract tests for the payloads and the prompt rules.

