## Mapping panel: vertical titles no longer turn Korean text upside down
================================================================================

Context:
The collapsed mapping-panel title (e.g. "공장") showed Korean glyphs upside
down while English read correctly. The title uses writing-mode: vertical-rl
plus a 180deg rotation. With text-orientation: mixed, CJK glyphs stay upright
before the rotation, so the rotation flips them.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/css/mapping.css
   Panel title text-orientation is sideways, so every script is laid on its
   side and the rotation reads bottom-to-top. Checked in Chrome with Korean
   and English labels.
2. tests/units/front/test_vertical_panel_title.py
   New contract test for the rule.

